Subject: [PATCH 7/7] Read-only answers for GUIs: players a click would take, the
 payment

Forge's own GUIs make every player avatar and every mana-pool symbol
clickable and let the running input refuse a useless click afterwards
(InputSelectTargets.onPlayerSelected shows "Cannot target this player",
InputPayMana.useManaFromPool does nothing). A GUI that offers only what
the input would accept, and shows the payment structured instead of
reading the prompt, needs the same answers beforehand:

- InputSelectTargets.isSelectablePlayer(Player): a chosen target (a click
  takes it back) or a player onPlayerSelected would take. Its checks moved
  unchanged, in the same order, into playerRefusal, which both use.
- InputPayMana.getRemainingManaCost(): the mana still to pay, exactly as
  getMessage shows it.
- InputPayMana.canUseManaFromPool(byte) with ManaPool.canPayCostWithColor:
  whether useManaFromPool would pay part of the cost. The search for the
  mana moved unchanged into ManaPool.manaToPayWithColor, which
  tryPayCostWithColor and the new check both use.
- InputPayMana.isSelectablePlayer(Player), in InputPayManaOfCostPayment the
  condition under which onPlayerSelected pays 2 life (Phyrexian mana,
  black mana payable with life).

No rule, card or AI behaviour changes: every new method only asks, and
the moved code runs as before.

Written for OpenMana on 2026-09-28.
